From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 88W8864: allocate the RX buffer size after the
 headroom

RX buffers were allocated with rx_buf_size bytes, then reserved
PCIE_MIN_BYTES_HEADROOM, and rx_buf_size bytes from skb->data were
mapped and announced to the firmware. The mapping extended 64 bytes past
the end of the buffer. Allocate room for rx_buf_size after the
headroom.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
[Robert Peerenboom: split out of neheb/mwlwifi (upstream branch) commit
 dcb73e4dca ("88W8864/88W8997: fix RX refill, TX status and teardown
 bugs") and backported to db97edf2 on top of the OpenWrt patches]
Signed-off-by: Robert Peerenboom <development@mindrush.de>
---
 hif/pcie/8864/rx.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/hif/pcie/8864/rx.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8864/rx.c
@@ -88,8 +88,12 @@ static int pcie_rx_ring_init(struct mwl_
 		for (i = 0; i < PCIE_MAX_NUM_RX_DESC; i++) {
 			rx_hndl = &desc->rx_hndl[i];
 			rx_hndl->pdesc = &desc->prx_ring[i];
+			/* The firmware may fill all of rx_buf_size after
+			 * the headroom.
+			 */
 			rx_hndl->psk_buff =
-				dev_alloc_skb(desc->rx_buf_size);
+				dev_alloc_skb(desc->rx_buf_size +
+					      PCIE_MIN_BYTES_HEADROOM);
 
 			if (!rx_hndl->psk_buff) {
 				wiphy_err(priv->hw->wiphy,
@@ -321,7 +325,8 @@ static inline int pcie_rx_refill(struct
 
 	desc = &pcie_priv->desc_data[0];
 
-	rx_hndl->psk_buff = dev_alloc_skb(desc->rx_buf_size);
+	rx_hndl->psk_buff = dev_alloc_skb(desc->rx_buf_size +
+					  PCIE_MIN_BYTES_HEADROOM);
 
 	if (!rx_hndl->psk_buff)
 		return -ENOMEM;
